id: jf-lyq6
title: Add bounded read-only Jellyfin API batches
description: "Add an agent-first manifest execution surface that resolves and preflights multiple exact Jellyfin OpenAPI read operations once, executes them deterministically through one authenticated client, and returns bounded structured results without permitting server mutations."
type: Plan
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[8]: agents,api,batch,contracts,openapi,read-only,release,tool-schema
created_at: "2026-07-25T22:29:31.042Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T00:19:46.403Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T00:19:45.774Z"
author: codex-jellyfin-batch
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: JSON manifests from a file or stdin preflight every request before target-operation execution and reject all non-read-only operations; Request count per-response size and aggregate response size are strictly bounded and deterministic ordered results preserve caller request identifiers; Dry-run emits resolved OpenAPI contracts without executing target operations; schema discovery remains a read-only contract fetch; TOON JSON YAML Markdown table and raw outputs plus function-calling schemas describe and validate the batch interface; Full release validation PM integrity private-data scans packaged consumer proof exact-head CI and terminal review inventory pass without publishing
definition_of_ready: Latest official Jellyfin release and OpenAPI sources verified; all-status PM duplicate search complete; private config permissions verified; existing exact-operation contracts understood.
goal: jf-mqpo
value: Let agents gather related Jellyfin facts safely in one deterministic invocation.
impact: Reduces repeated schema fetches and process overhead while making multi-operation automation preflightable and bounded.
outcome: A production-ready read-only batch API contract complementing typed commands and exact single-operation execution.
why_now: "All 429 live operations are individually reachable, but multi-step agent workflows still require repetitive process orchestration and cannot preflight a complete read plan."
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: github-review-bots
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11
release: next-manual-release
resolution: "Implemented and reviewed bounded read-only API batch execution with whole-manifest preflight, exact OpenAPI resolution, strict budgets, deterministic outputs, schemas, docs, live acceptance, and no publication."
expected_result: "Agents can submit a bounded manifest of exact GET HEAD or OPTIONS operations, reject the full plan before target execution when invalid, and consume schema-valid ordered results without modifying Jellyfin data."
actual_result: "The CLI provides jf api batch with file or stdin input, dry-run contracts, 25-request default and 100-request hard ceiling, one-MiB per-response and ten-MiB aggregate defaults, all output formats, 181 compiled live read-only acceptances, installed consumer proof, and fully dispositioned PR findings."
