comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:29:31.042Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"All 42 PM items, their statuses and rich recent lineage, project graph, latest official Jellyfin 10.11.11 release, live sanitized 429-operation schema, configured profile permissions, and current GitHub head were reviewed. No duplicate batch-execution item exists."
  "2026-07-25T22:48:55.403Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"Implementation validation so far: 14 focused Bun tests and 20 focused portable tests pass; compiled live batch returned 2/2 ordered successes; isolated npm-installed jf-cli resolved from an unrelated prefix and passed dry-run plus live batch. Full release validation, audits, and Trivy are green. Honest repository baselines are 39.84 statements, 40.13 branches, 51.10 functions, 39.45 lines and 8.44 percent duplicated lines, so canonical P0 items jf-mkzh and jf-lpki remain open and are not represented as complete."
  "2026-07-25T22:55:33.015Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"PM linked-test result: focused and live commands passed (14/14 and 181/181). validate:release reached the final changelog check after all tests/build/package/security smokes, then reproduced known core pm-cli issue #682 because the tracker sandbox has 43/43 items but lacks source Git tag identity. Direct source-workspace validation is being rerun; no duplicate upstream issue will be filed."
  "2026-07-25T23:25:15.264Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"CodeRabbit exact-head review produced five valid findings. Accepted all: clarify PM request-count bound, document the complete GET/HEAD/OPTIONS allowlist, name input-selection booleans, parse manifests before OpenAPI I/O, and validate dry-run output against api_batch_plan. Added docstrings to all new source helpers while applying the fixes."
  "2026-07-25T23:28:32.348Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"The CodeRabbit review summary contained a sixth actionable finding outside the diff: HEAD and 204 responses must short-circuit before declared content-length enforcement. Accepted it, moved the guard below the bodyless-response return, and added a regression test for a large declared HEAD representation with a one-byte response budget."
  "2026-07-25T23:31:05.264Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"PR #40: https://github.com/unbraind/jellyfin-cli/pull/40 . Exact reviewed head before tracker closeout: 2431439f08514ba7678f9d5822ce3c9f10ad4d1a. Final tracker/changelog commit will retrigger required checks and bot inventory before merge."
  "2026-07-25T23:31:46.114Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"Closeout generation exposed package.json pinning changelog PM execution to 2026.7.24-3. Updated the deterministic npm-exec pin to current 2026.7.25, matching the installed global CLI and managed pm-changelog package."
  "2026-07-26T00:18:52.537Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"Final exact-head CodeRabbit review reported five actionable hardening findings: exact managed-extension provenance pin, precise target-operation preflight wording, shared numeric defaults, successful exit-code assertions across formatter tests, and portable stdin EPIPE handling. All are accepted for implementation before merge."
  "2026-07-26T00:19:45.103Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"Implemented all five final-review findings. pm install npm:pm-changelog@2026.7.25 replaced replayable latest provenance through the managed extension lifecycle; README now distinguishes schema-fetch I/O from target-operation preflight; batch defaults share named constants; the formatter matrix asserts all exit codes; and the Node portable stdin adapter consumes expected early-exit stream errors. Focused Bun and portable suites pass 14/14 each."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:29:31.042Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"Privacy boundary: credentials, server address, entity IDs, raw live responses, and cached OpenAPI documents remain only in environment variables and owner-only ~/.jellyfin-cli. PM, git, CI, PRs, and summaries may contain only public versions, aggregate counts, and synthetic fixtures."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:55:35.102Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,"For stdin CLI behavior under portable Vitest, the Node Bun.spawn compatibility adapter must explicitly pipe Blob input; Bun-native success alone is insufficient cross-runtime evidence."
  "2026-07-25T22:55:42.543Z",codex-jellyfin-batch,Validate explicitly supplied official artifact identifiers before fetching a live baseline. Early syntactic and prerelease-policy rejection prevents unnecessary authenticated probes and makes security tests deterministic under host load.
